0..76 Comment "//! A case on a vector checks each arm at the fields of its own constructor."
77..80 Comment "//!"
81..159 Comment "//! A case on an indexed family checks each constructor arm at its own fields."
160..215 Comment "//! `oneLength` writes an arm that no index can select."
216..255 Comment "//! `vector-head.gandr` omits that arm."
256..259 Comment "//!"
260..333 Comment "//! An arm may return a constructor at a length that a call computes. The"
334..407 Comment "//! `VCons` arm of `vappend` returns `VCons` at `plus(m, Succ(k))`, which"
408..452 Comment "//! computes the length that `VCons` states."
453..456 Comment "//!"
457..537 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families] — a case that checks each arm at"
538..572 Comment "//!   its own constructor\'s fields"
573..651 Comment "//! - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
652..678 Comment "//!   the length it states"
679..682 Comment "//!"
683..784 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308 \"Dybjer, Inductive families\""
786..823 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
